25-04-28T13:44:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T17:14:14Z","closed_at":"2026-09-08T17:14:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in:\n- v4.5.dev3.official [28089c40c]\n- master [1b4ed4c03]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev3 - Nobara Linux 41 (KDE Plasma) on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 (nvidia; 570.133.07) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a normal map with generated mipmaps, it does not render correctly at the seams of the model, especially when the UVs are stacked/the mesh is mirrored, which is a common technique to save texture space.\n\nThe error is subtle but visible along the middle of the model. The flat surface no longer looks seamless.\nThis error is exacerbated when attempting to use EXR textures (See #105867), which is one of the ways I thought it may be possible to fix this.\n\n**Disabling the \"Normal Map\" import option for the texture prevents this regardless of \"High Quality\" being enabled or not but this is not an ideal solution.**\n\n| No mipmaps | Mipmaps |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89012d93-092b-43a0-a731-7df324c30287) | ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7d98fce0-daf2-42dd-a2b4-c85ceae42621) |\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download the MRP\n2. Observe that the model looks incorrect where the seams meet.\n3. Set the filtering method on the model's material to `Linear` and observe that it now displays correctly.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19940962/normal_mipmaps.zip)","closed_by":{"log